notes:
These are the primary sources the csoh.org kill chain cites. Every fact about the incident in this deck comes from that page, which draws on these.

Mandiant's write-up, on Google Cloud's blog, covers the software supply chain compromise. 3CX's Mandiant security update covers the initial intrusion vector. MITRE ATT&CK tracks the activity as Campaign C0057. The page lists a ReversingLabs article as First cascading supply chain compromise. MITRE's page for T1553.002, Code Signing, defines the technique the page maps to stage 04. Volexity reported EDR and antivirus vendors flagging the updates as early as March 22, 2023, and CrowdStrike reported the signed app beaconing on March 29.

The background slides name their own sources: MITRE ATT&CK, and the csoh.org Zero Trust page and glossary.

